    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a650edde_1752f0e7",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1064128
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:27:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t touched kernel code in \u003e5 years, so I\u0027ll have some rather basic questions on kernel CLs.\n\nI want to check here: do `static_branch_disable()` and `static_branch_enable()` only impact the current thread or current stack? We\u0027ll want to make sure we don\u0027t disable `init_on_alloc` globally.",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cab0d32_de4d8439",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020578
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T21:05:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately it\u0027s a global setting. The balloon code does re-enable this once the allocation call completes, however, any allocations happening while this flag is turned off, will not be considered \"security-hardened\".\n\nWe should also considered the impact on those allocations and whether the hardening impact from `init_on_alloc` is absolutely necessary in all cases.\n\nThe other approach is to introduce a new GFP flag for allocation that reverts the effect of `init_on_alloc`. This would scope the impact to the specific allocation. This will introduce more changes in the core mm/ code to maintain until we get an upstream resolution.\n\nI feel like this idea might make more sense upstream. Rather than code opt-in using `__GFP_ZERO`, an opt-out with `__GFP_NO_ZERO` would help audit the code easier. As I said in another comment, we should raise the underlying root cause in upstream mailing list and ask for a better resolution.",
      "parentUuid": "a650edde_1752f0e7",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dce3ee63_bd616f7e",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1064128
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T21:16:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should get security reviewers to take a look at this if it\u0027s decreasing our hardening.\n\nOtherwise a `__GFP_NO_ZERO` flag makes sense to do this in a more targeted way.",
      "parentUuid": "8cab0d32_de4d8439",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26854d91_5947f03b",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020578
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T21:30:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added oysteine@ to take a look at the security impact.\n\nSo far, the changes related to flex memory in the kernel have been limited to the virtio-balloon code. I tried to keep this patch similarly constrained in that respect. There\u0027s not a lot of code to be added for a new GFP flag. The question is if we are ok with the additional maintenance cost that spreads to core kernel code. Do you have thoughts on what the ongoing burden cost and how that might be impacted?",
      "parentUuid": "dce3ee63_bd616f7e",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1d67442_acc4a8f0",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1064128
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T23:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not too concerned with the maintenance cost since we only upgrade kernels ~once per year and you say that the changes would be small. I\u0027d lean towards making the more secure change, but I don\u0027t have a strong opinion there and will defer to oysteine@ on how important this is.\n\nIdeally the change is upstreamed since it seems to impact other devices too. That would alleviate some amount of the maintenance burden, at least in the long term.",
      "parentUuid": "26854d91_5947f03b",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3354be7e_d4206921",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020578
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-22T21:59:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated the change by introducing the `__GFP_NO_INIT_ON_ALLOC` flag.\n\nThis commit is a good candidate for an upstream RFC to start the conversation.",
      "parentUuid": "f1d67442_acc4a8f0",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bc774b8_c8d995dc",
        "filename": "mm/balloon_compaction.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1064128
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T15:51:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks good to me, especially as a starting point for conversation upstream.\n\nIt\u0027s likely better to split into two CLs: one for adding the new GFP flag and one for using it in virtio-balloon.",
      "parentUuid": "3354be7e_d4206921",
      "revId": "9f76aee1b9dffbad9ae1193ff05b1d64090c307a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
